AWS Cloud Engineer Interview Prep | 0–2 Years Experience

If you’re a fresher or early-career AWS Cloud Engineer (0–2 years) preparing for interviews, here are must-know AWS interview questions to test and strengthen your fundamentals 👇

🔹 AWS Interview Questions (0–2 Years)


What is cloud computing and what are its benefits?
What are the different cloud service models (IaaS, PaaS, SaaS)?
What is AWS and why is it popular?
Explain AWS Global Infrastructure.
What is an AWS Region and Availability Zone?
What is an AMI?
What is EC2 and its use cases?
What are the different EC2 instance types?
What is the difference between EBS and Instance Store?
What is S3 and what are its storage classes?
What is the difference between S3 and EBS?
What is IAM and why is it important?
Difference between IAM User, Group, Role, and Policy.
What is a Security Group?
What is a Network ACL?
Difference between Security Group and NACL.
What is VPC?
What is a Subnet (public vs private)?
What is an Internet Gateway?
What is a NAT Gateway?
What is Elastic Load Balancer (ELB)?
What are the types of Load Balancers in AWS?
What is Auto Scaling and why is it used?
What is CloudWatch?
What is CloudTrail?
What is Route 53?
What is RDS and supported database engines?
Difference between RDS and DynamoDB.
What is AWS Shared Responsibility Model?
How do you secure AWS resources?

